cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SentinelAgent Realtime"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its method, please cite it. If you cite a NUMBER from it, cite the
  commit as well: every figure regenerates from the committed verdict files, and a commit hash is
  what makes that check possible for a reader.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rajelli
    given-names: Rahul
repository-code: "https://github.com/RahulRajelli/sentinel-realtime"
abstract: >-
  A realtime flight-anomaly detector for ArduPilot telemetry, plus an evaluation harness that
  measures whether an LLM judge can name the ROOT CAUSE of a fault rather than the first symptom
  that fired. Its central construction is a fault scenario on which a free deterministic baseline
  is wrong by construction rather than by measurement: a detector persistence gate places the
  causal advisory 1.0 s AFTER the symptom it produced, so the rule "the first alarm after
  something changed is the cause" scores 0.00 and any costlier method must earn its cost against
  a baseline that cannot be tuned into agreement.
keywords:
  - uav
  - ardupilot
  - mavlink
  - root-cause-analysis
  - llm-evaluation
  - agent-evaluation
  - baseline-design
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
